    <string name="ui_1_select_your_apps_or_add_contacts_if_you__317" formatted="false">"1. Select your apps or add contacts. If you have no widgets yet, the creator opens automatically.\n\n2. Adjust icons, shadows, titles and background. Tap “Add to home screen” and confirm in Android.\n\n3. Tap an app to open it, or a contact to view their details and call them from there. Touch and hold the widget on your home screen to resize it.\n\nIn the preview, drag to reorder or tap × to remove a shortcut.\n\nThe app theme and notification access are in Options in the top bar. Each widget keeps its own settings.\n\nContacts: use “Refresh photos” to reload images for contacts you have added. Android may ask for read access to their photos. You can use initials without that permission.\n\nYou can also add widgets from the Android widget picker: find “Foldery.2.AI”. To remove a widget, remove it from your home screen.\n\nOnly personal profile apps are included. Some apps or manufacturers limit notifications. Badges are optional and may differ from unread messages."</string>
